*The type of grenades thrown depends on whether the ability key (default {{Keybind|1}}) was tapped or held.
**'''Tap''' to throw '''Shrapnel Vortex''' grenades.
**'''Hold''' to throw '''Shield Satellite''' grenades.
**Tap/Hold control behavior can be inverted in the Options menu.

<div class="tabber-borderless" ><tabber>
|-|Shrapnel Vortex=<div style="display:none;">'''Shrapnel Vortex'''<br /></div>

* '''Tap''' the ability key to scatter <u>'''3'''</u> grenades horizontally offset from the reticle by <u>'''-45°'''</u>, <u>'''0°'''</u>, and <u>'''+45°'''</u> in the '''Shrapnel Vortex''' configuration.  Each grenade will bounce off of surfaces and objects until they land on a horizontal surface, where it will release a vortex of flying shrapnel for {{Stat|Ability Duration|icon=only}}'''13''' seconds. Each shrapnel vortex has a {{Stat|Ability Range|icon=only}}'''2 / 3 / 4 / 5''' meter radius, inflicts {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''200 / 250 / 350 / 500''' {{D|Slash}} damage per second with a <u>'''33%'''</u> status chance, and a <u>'''100%'''</u> chance to stagger enemies slightly or strongly on each tick.
** Shrapnel Vortexes do '''not''' require line of sight to damage and stun enemies within range.
* Shrapnel grenade uses a custom model that resembles the shape and pattern of a baseball. When deployed, the grenade spins rapidly in place while emitting a glow of energy particles.
* Shrapnel Vortex visually creates a sphere consisting of multiple trails of energy particles that encircle the grenade at high speed.

|-|Shield Satellite=<div style="display:none;">'''Shield Satellite'''<br /></div>

* '''Hold''' down the ability key to scatter <u>'''4'''</u> grenades horizontally offset from the reticle by <u>'''-45°'''</u>, <u>'''-25°'''</u>, <u>'''+25°'''</u>, and <u>'''+45°'''</u> in the '''Shield Satellite''' configuration. Each grenade will bounce off of surfaces and objects until they land on a horizontal surface, where it will release a floating shield satellite with a lifetime of <u>'''13'''</u> seconds. The satellite will attach to the <u>'''first'''</u> nearest ally without an attached satellite that comes within {{Stat|Ability Range|icon=only}}'''2 / 3 / 4 / 5''' meters of it and instantly restore {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''200 / 300 / 400 / 500''' [[shield]] points to them. While attached, it constantly provides {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''25 / 30 / 40 / 50''' shield points per second for the ally, capping at their [[Overshields]] limit. If the ally's [[Shield#Shield Gating|shield gate]] is triggered while it is attached, the satellite will grant <u>'''2x'''</u> minimum shield gate invincibility duration and immediately terminate.
** Satellites do '''not''' require line of sight to be picked up by allies in range.
** Each satellite's pickup radius will briefly appear when first deployed. While standing outside of the pickup radius, active satellites appear surrounded by an energy sphere to guide allies toward them.
** Shield points per second is constant throughout a satellite's lifetime, allowing shields and overshields to regenerate immediately following damage.
** Eligible allies for satellite attachment include: Protea, other Warframes, [[Companions]], [[Eidolon Lure]]s, summoned allied units such as [[Specter]]s, allied [[Invasion]] units, [[Rescue|Hostages]], [[Kavor Defector]]s, [[Sortie]] and [[Arbitrations]] Defense Operatives, and [[Defense Objects]] coming into the satellite's range.
***Does '''not''' apply to [[Excavator]]s.
** Has no effect on {{WF|Inaros}},  {{WF|Kullervo}}, or {{WF|Nidus}} due to their lack of shields.
* Shield satellite uses a custom model that resembles a spherical device with visible mechanical parts. When deployed on the ground, the satellite floats and weaves around the air several meters above while an energy stream anchors it to the surface.
* Shield satellites visually orbit their target in a steady clockwise motion, directly facing it while funneling an energy stream to reinforce shields, represented by a translucent cluster of connected hexagons.
